course: dictionary
lesson: 13760
title: Stepping in between
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. They sound grown-up and you mostly meet them in older books, rules and exam papers. Interpose is one of these words. You can still work it out from the words around it.
explain: «The referee tried to interpose himself between the two boys who were fighting.» The clues are fighting and tried to stop it, so interpose must mean to step in between them. Test it: "stepped in between the two boys" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Interpose can also mean to interrupt. «Mia wanted to interpose a question, but the teacher was still speaking.» Mia wanted to break in with her question while someone else was talking. The word between or into the middle of a moment is the clue.
fact: «Interpose» means to place something between two things or people.
fact: To interpose yourself means to step in between people, often to stop a fight.
fact: To interpose a remark means to interrupt by saying something.
fact: Interpose is a formal word, so you will mostly find it in older books, legal texts and exam writing.
fact: Interpose, interposes, interposed and interposing are all forms of the same verb.
exercise: «The guard interposed himself between the crowd and the gate.» What does interposed mean here? | Gave a present to | Ran away from | Shouted at | *Stepped in between
exercise: «Mia wanted to interpose a question, but the teacher was still speaking.» What does interpose a question mean? | Answer every question on the test | Write a question down quietly for later | Forget the question | *Break in with a question while someone else is talking
exercise: «The tall wall was interposed between the house and the road.» What does interposed mean? | Moved far away | Painted green | Knocked down | *Placed between
test: «The big umbrella was interposed between the rain and the picnic.» What does interposed suggest? | Made louder | *Placed between two things to block something | Folded up for later | Lost in the rain
test: «Ben interposed a remark about the ending, and the whole class turned to look.» What did Ben do? | Fell asleep in class | Wrote the ending himself | Left the room quietly | *Interrupted by saying something
exam: Which sentence uses interposed correctly? | Tom and Sam laughed about the joke | The cake was interposed for a quick dance | The sun interposed a happy song | *Nina interposed herself between the two angry dogs
